not delete user\\nhistory to pass scans. Stop if a second production path remains reachable.\\n\\n\\n\\n--- BEGIN APPROVED IMMUTABLE PATCH OVERLAY ---\\nPatch ID: P-N40-001\\nReason: N40's own prior result report disclosed that tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py tests the retired Plan 25 parser_for/--lab-id CLI surface and fails to import against the new build_parser()-based CLI, but the file was outside N40's write set at the time. The write set now includes it (ownership correction); N40 must retire/rewrite the stale assertions rather than leaving a downstream node to route around a collection-blocking import error it did not cause.\\nExpected effect: tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py imports cleanly and asserts the Plan 26 migration contract (parser_for absent, legacy flags rejected, no Plan 25 symbols reachable) instead of the retired Plan 25 dispatch behavior, unblocking pytest -q tests/runtime collection for all downstream full-suite runs\\nInstructions:\\nOwnership correction. This node's own prior result report already disclosed,\\ncorrectly and explicitly, that `tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py` tests\\nthe retired Plan 25 CLI surface (`parser_for(runtime)`, `--lab-id` dispatch to\\na mocked `CurriculumFactoryGraph`/`CodexWorker`) and fails to import against\\nthe new CLI, but was out of this node's write set at the time so it could not\\nbe fixed. That file is now in this node's write set. Retire/rewrite it here,\\nas the node whose CLI cutover the file's own assertions have gone stale\\nagainst.\\n\\n`tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py` currently has two independent parts:\\n\\n1. `RunCurriculumParserTests` and its shared top-of-file import\\n   `from runtime.run_curriculum import main, parser_for` \\u2014 this is what is\\n   broken. `parser_for` no longer exists; `run_curriculum.py` now exposes only\\n   `build_parser()` (no arguments, a different and much smaller flag surface:\\n   `--engine-root`, `--curriculum`, `--output-root`, one of\\n   `--preflight`/`--unit`/`--all`/`--resume`, `--authorization`). Replace this\\n   class with new tests asserting the Plan 26 migration contract instead of\\n   testing removed behavior:\\n   - `parser_for` remains absent: importing it from `runtime.run_curriculum`\\n     fails (e.g. `assertRaises(ImportError)` around the import, or\\n     `assertFalse(hasattr(run_curriculum_module, \\\"parser_for\\\"))`).\\n   - Legacy CLI surfaces remain rejected: flags the old parser accepted\\n     (`--lab-id`, and the old per-lab/per-run policy flags such as\\n     `--max-model-calls-per-lab`, `--max-concurrency`,\\n     `--max-meta-revision-cycles`, `--retry-malformed-output`) are not\\n     recognized by the current `build_parser()` and raise `SystemExit(2)`\\n     when passed.\\n   - `runtime/run_curriculum.py` uses only the Plan 26 LangGraph path: no\\n     Plan 25 symbol (`CurriculumFactoryGraph`, `CodexWorker`, `GeminiReviewer`,\\n     `runtime.controller.CurriculumRuntime`, `runtime.session_bridge`, or\\n     `parser_for`) is imported or referenced by the module. Prefer a static\\n     check (e.g. AST or source inspection of `runtime/run_curriculum.py`),\\n     consistent with the import-audit style already used in\\n     `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py`, over importing those symbols into the\\n     test itself.\\n   Do not restore `parser_for`, `CurriculumFactoryGraph`, `CodexWorker`, or any\\n   Plan 25 dispatch path in `runtime/run_curriculum.py` to make old assertions\\n   pass. The old behavior is retired; the test must assert that it stays\\n   retired, not resurrect it.\\n\\n2. `RunCurriculumElapsedTimeTests` \\u2014 this class does not import or use\\n   `parser_for`/`main` at all; it drives `runtime.controller.CurriculumRuntime\\n   .simulate(...)` directly, a historical module this node's own migration\\n   disposition deliberately left in place and unreachable from the production\\n   CLI (see this node's existing result report, \\\"Migration disposition\\\"