{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdyrcN4MQgSNhbHnc2VVP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011pVFbwgCbk1XyhjSfy4e3T","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Independent invariant + spec traceability audit","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"You are doing an independent, read-only verification pass for a final audit (N90) of \"Plan 26\", a LangGraph-based curriculum-factory production system. You have NOT seen any prior conversation about this — verify everything from source directly, do not trust any prose claim without checking the actual code/spec.\n\nRepo root: /Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder\nKey locations:\n- Spec: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/spec/langgraph_curriculum_factory.spec.v1.md\n- QA criteria: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/qa_criteria.v3.md\n- Implementation graph: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/implementation.graph.v3.yaml\n- Traceability matrix: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/contracts/traceability_matrix.v1.md\n- Node ownership matrix: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/contracts/node_ownership.v1.md\n- Production runtime code: runtime/langgraph_factory/*.py, runtime/run_curriculum.py\n- Tests: tests/runtime/*.py\n\nPlease verify and report on EACH of these 8 invariant classes, citing exact file:line evidence for each (not paraphrase of a doc — read the actual code):\n\n1. **Eight model jobs**: exactly 8 model jobs are defined (M01-M08 or similar), prompts/schemas are loaded package-relative (not cwd-relative), and the count is enforced somewhere in code (not just documented).\n2. **Authority**: routing/join/acceptance/terminal decisions are made ONLY from a code-controlled state/guard, never from a field a model output could set. Find the mechanism that rejects model-proposed control fields (e.g. a FORBIDDEN_MODEL_FIELDS-style list or schema validation).\n3. **Denominators**: fan-out/join counting (e.g. \"how many source files\", \"how many visual members\") is recomputed fresh by code each time, not trusted from a model claim or cached blindly; stale/extra/cross-unit members are rejected.\n4. **Repair**: repair/patch admission recomputes the diff itself, rejects a stale parent hash, and hard-fails on any out-of-boundary file/pointer touch.\n5. **Persistence/resume**: checkpointing uses a real LangGraph checkpointer (e.g. SqliteSaver), and resume validates against drift (identity, frozen digest, executable hash, evidence, accepted bytes) before resuming; resume is refused outside allowed terminal states.\n6. **Terminals**: enumerate the exact terminal states the system can reach. Confirm terminal-writing code independently re-derives/validates the terminal rather than trusting an upstream claim, and downgrades unsupported/inconsistent claims to a system-failure terminal.\n7. **CLI**: confirm there is exactly ONE live production execution path (one function that builds the compiled LangGraph graph, called from exactly the fresh-run and resume-run branches of the CLI, nothing else) — cite the call sites. Confirm no simulation/session-bridge/legacy-Plan-25 code is reachable from that path.\n8. Separately: confirm there is exactly one `StateGraph(...)` construction and one `.compile(...)` call anywhere in `runtime/langgraph_factory/*.py`, and that no `langchain`, `langchain_openai`, `langchain_google_genai`, `openai`, or `google.generativeai` package is imported anywhere under `runtime/` (langchain_core is fine, it's LangGraph's own dependency).\n\nAlso: skim the spec file's normative \"must\"/\"shall\" requirements (roughly sections 0-21) and the qa_criteria.v3.md file, and tell me if you find ANY requirement that has no corresponding implementation you can locate (a real gap), versus everything being traceable to actual code you found. Don't try to build an exhaustive line-by-line matrix — spend your effort sampling for red flags (e.g. TODO markers, `NotImplementedError`, requirements that reference nonexistent functions).\n\nReport each of the 8 items as PASS/FAIL/UNCLEAR with a one-line file:line citation, plus a short list of any spec/QA gaps found. Keep the total report under 600 words — cite paths and line numbers, not long code quotes.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1363,"cache_read_input_tokens":96164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1363},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70617d74-9007-4f2b-b1d2-c9e4e0acc97a","uuid":"9b2052f1-5cd8-4468-bc30-37b766fd8ed1","timestamp":"2026-08-13T01:10:41.149Z","request_id":"req_011CdyrcM9HTuBtysncDHqRk"}
