{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0146PCYw7skrMPsrKtns6bRP","type":"tool_result","content":"4:vs. model routing, boundary-checked admission, and retest dispatch. Shared by the\n6:`repair_requests`-shaped state (spec section 12's boundary/diff/invalidation-DAG\n18:`{finding_id, evidence_key, owner, boundary, parent_hash, fingerprint}` shape.\n61:    \"within_boundary\",\n206:def finding_fingerprint(owner: str, boundary: Sequence[str], message: Any) -> str:\n209:    Keyed on owner, boundary pointers, and message -- not on `finding_id` (which\n215:    return canonical_digest({\"owner\": owner, \"boundary\": sorted(boundary), \"message\": str(message)})\n251:                \"invalid_input\", \"finding declares no boundary pointer\",\n256:        parent_hash = parent_head.get(\"hash\") if isinstance(parent_head, Mapping) else None\n268:                \"boundary\": pointer,\n269:                \"parent_hash\": parent_hash,\n297:        key = str(finding.get(\"boundary\", \"\")).strip(\"/\").split(\"/\")[-1]\n335:def within_boundary(pointer: str, allowed: Sequence[str]) -> bool:\n336:    \"\"\"Whether ``pointer`` is exactly, or nested under, one declared boundary pointer.\"\"\"\n574:    boundary_pointers = sorted({finding[\"boundary\"] for finding in selected[\"findings\"]})\n575:    parent_hash = next(\n576:        (finding[\"parent_hash\"] for finding in selected[\"findings\"] if finding.get(\"parent_hash\")),\n591:        \"boundary\": {\"json_pointers\": boundary_pointers},\n592:        \"parent_hash\": parent_hash,\n647:    \"\"\"Apply a code-owned, boundary-scoped correction to the parent body.\n658:    for pointer in request[\"boundary\"][\"json_pointers\"]:\n662:                f\"deterministic repair has no admitted fact for boundary pointer {pointer!r}\",\n730:                        \"pointer\": finding[\"boundary\"],\n742:                \"boundary\": request[\"boundary\"],\n811:        \"key\", \"stream\", \"version\", \"parent_hash\", \"hash\", \"record_kind\",\n825:    uniformly here is what lets D19's boundary-scoped JSON-pointer patch and\n826:    D20's diff/boundary check apply to a channel regardless of which\n883:    \"\"\"Admit a boundary-checked child atomically, or refuse it as a system fault.\n886:    `changed_path_manifest`: a diff pointer outside the declared boundary, or a\n889:    routed repairable finding, because a boundary violation is a build/model\n904:    boundary = request[\"boundary\"][\"json_pointers\"]\n940:        \"the repair candidate's declared parent is not the current head (stale repair)\",\n946:    out_of_bound = sorted(pointer for pointer in diff if not within_boundary(pointer, boundary))\n950:        \"a repair candidate changed bytes outside its declared boundary\",\n951:        stream=stream, out_of_bound=out_of_bound, boundary=boundary,\n957:        \"parent_hash\": current_hash,\n987:            stream: {\"version\": child_record[\"version\"], \"parent_hash\": child_record[\"parent_hash\"], \"hash\": child_record[\"hash\"]}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011pVFbwgCbk1XyhjSfy4e3T","session_id":"70617d74-9007-4f2b-b1d2-c9e4e0acc97a","uuid":"9372727e-3815-4c21-b984-a08fd3058631","timestamp":"2026-08-13T01:11:21.223Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Independent invariant + spec traceability audit"}
